#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Remark]
// #title[Title]

The #local("00GQ")[Type of General Cartesian Decompositions] of the empty type is not a set.

#proof[
  Let $S -= emptyset$. Let $A$ be a type with more than one element, say $A -= "Bool"$. Let $e$ be the unique equivalence $e : A xx emptyset ~= emptyset$. 
  Then $(emptyset,A,e)$ is a point in  "cart-dec"(S). By #local("00DY")[Lemma 00DY] its loop space is characterized as. 
  $
    "Eq-cart-dec"(S)((emptyset, A,e),(emptyset,A,e)) -= sum_(f : 0 ~= 0) sum_(g : A ~= A) e @ (f xx g) ~ e
  $
Notice that type of homotopies $e @ (f xx g) ~ e$ is contractible, since the domain of the functions involved is $emptyset$. So is the type $(0 ~= 0)$.
Therefor
$
  ((emptyset, A,e)=(emptyset,A,e)) ~= (A ~= A)
$
Since we chose $A$ to be $"Bool"$, the right hand side is not contractible, so 
$"cart-dec"(emptyset)$ is not a set.
]


